# Inspector fields

Unity inspector-tunable fields are `public`. Do not use `[SerializeField]` on private fields. This is the project-wide standard for new and edited C# files.

```csharp
// BAD
[SerializeField, Min(2)] private int _columns = 5;

// GOOD
[Min(2)] public int _columns = 5;
```

Keep:

- `private` for runtime-only state that must not appear in the Inspector
- `_underscore` prefix on fields (public inspector fields included)
- `[SerializeReference]` for polymorphic serialized types — public alone is not enough
- Other inspector attributes (`Header`, `Min`, `Range`, `Required`, `SubclassSelector`, etc.)

Do not mass-convert existing `[SerializeField] private` fields in unrelated files unless asked.
